    {
      "id": "d1fe8bb4-71fb-40e2-b989-4f4fbd7b239f",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -5072,
        2288
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 700,
        "height": 840,
        "content": "# 📥 Inbox Autopilot (Ollama)\n\nTriage your inbox with a **local, private** LLM — no API keys, no per-token cost. Unread Gmail is classified, action items are extracted, a reply is drafted, and **you approve it from Telegram**. On approval a **draft reply lands back in Gmail, in-thread** — a human always sends the final message.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Ingest & classify** — unread emails are pulled from **Gmail**, then the Classifier tags each as `urgent`, `action_needed`, `fyi`, or `spam`.\n2. **Route** — only `urgent` / `action_needed` mail moves on; the rest is marked *skipped*.\n3. **Extract & draft** — the Extractor pulls the task + deadline, then the Drafter writes a short reply.\n4. **Approve → reply → log** — Telegram sends the summary + draft to approve/reject. On approval a **threaded draft reply** is created in Gmail and the email is labeled; every decision is logged to Google Sheets.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install **Ollama** and run `ollama pull llama3.1`. Make sure n8n can reach it (default `http://localhost:11434`).\n2. Connect your **Gmail** account on *Get Unread Emails* (the draft + label nodes reuse it).\n3. Add credentials to both **Ollama Chat Model** nodes.\n4. Connect your **Telegram** bot and set your `chatId`.\n5. Connect **Google Sheets** and pick your Decision Log sheet.\n6. Click **Test workflow** to triage the current unread batch.\n\n### Customization\n- *Label as Triaged* stars the email by default — swap in a custom **Triaged** label and set the fetch to `is:unread -is:starred` to stop re-processing.\n- Change the Gmail search filter, category list, or reply tone in each chain's prompt.\n- Swap the Manual Trigger for a **Gmail Trigger** to run automatically."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
